<title>UK: SBC sets warrants on sterling/mark exchange rate.</title>
<headline>SBC sets warrants on sterling/mark exchange rate.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Schweizerischer Bankverein (Deutschland) AG has issued 50 million American-style call and put warrants, in five equal tranches, on the sterling/mark exhange rate, lead manager SBC Warburg said.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> EXERCISE PERIOD 20.DEC.96-15.SEP.97   PAYDATE	19.DEC.96</p>
<p> LISTING	   FFURT, DUSS	     MIN EXER LOT 100</p>
<p>SPOT REFERENCE  2.5597 DEM</p>
<p>* * * * * *</p>
<p> TYPE  STRIKE    ISSUE     PREMIUM    GEARING</p>
<p> CALL  2.55 DEM  5.21 DEM  1.66 PCT   49.13 X</p>
<p> PUT   2.55 DEM  10.40 DEM 4.44 PCT   24.61 X</p>
<p> CALL  2.60 DEM  3.50 DEM  2.94 PCT   73.13 X</p>
<p> PUT   2.60 DEM  13.90 DEM 3.86 PCT   18.42 X</p>
<p> CALL  2.65 DEM  2.28 DEM  4.42 PCT   112.27 X</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
